  "behavior": [
    "Inventory-v3 retains exact original known native-journal, attempt-ledger and snapshot custody attribute bytes and SHA256 on their actual descriptors. The selected root nonce remains separately recorded and externally bound.",
    "Required explicit limits bound total owner attributes to10000 and value bytes to16MiB; individual known owner values are at most4096bytes. Encoded entries have a60MiB ceiling within the64MiB evidence reader limit.",
    "Unknown or malformed user.urnetwork.* names refuse a complete report; unchanged file bytes cannot hide a missing or changed owner attribute during verification.",
    "Observation failures and cancellation refuse current admission without inferring identity loss; changed metadata during traversal poisons that snapshot generation. Closed caller descriptors remain caller errors.",
    "Explicit rebound comparison still requires a separately approved target root declaration and exact opaque original owner metadata; report restart_authorized staysfalse."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "57 selected durablevolume roots pass normal/race and peer package vet; no full Connect or downstream consumer/release claim.",
    "Only the reviewed owner namespace and existing file mode/uid/gid/content fields are covered; arbitrary ACL/security/non-owner extended metadata is outside this report.",
    "Owner values are opaque; this package does not authenticate protocol signatures, validate owner head semantics, rebind embedded physical inodes, repair pending commits or authorize writer restart.",
    "Production CLI adoption of the two new limit fields, offline provisioning/restore application and independent source rerun remain separate pending scopes.",
    "No live mount, signing, chain broadcast, deployment or production service start. Prior6cd/v2 and consumer receipts remain immutable."
  ],
